            <h2>Wildlife and Natural Wonders</h2>

            <p>The Galapagos Islands have long been known as a living laboratory of evolution. Visitors may spot giant tortoises in the highlands, frolicsome sea lions along the shore, and schools of bright fish beneath clear waters. No other place on the planet compares in terms of species diversity. </p>

            <p>All the islands have a variation in their landscape and ecosystem. Some have dramatic lava fields, and others have sandy beaches or lush landscapes. A trip on a cruise to Galapagos Islands brings this diversity into play within an unspoiled journey of discovery. </p>

